        "y0": 0.5542862232779098,
        "x1": 0.6804689075630252,
        "y1": 0.5768456057007125
      },
      "text": "⇐⇒ 1 − λr |∇w1| Φ(x,λ|∇w1|) − λr−1Φ(x,|∇w1|) = 0.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.09519159663865547,
        "y0": 0.5788337292161521,
        "x1": 0.9052453781512605,
        "y1": 0.6133301662707838
      },
      "text": "Therefore we may have λ = 1 and the equality holds. If λ = 1 then ∇w1(x) = 0 or Φ(x,λ|∇w1|) = λr−1Φ(x,|∇w1|) for a.a. x ∈ Ω. This disjunction is equivalent to the second relation since Φ(x,0) = 0.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.4215126050420168,
        "y0": 0.6060665083135393,
        "x1": 0.47136974789915964,
        "y1": 0.6336009501187649
      },
      "text": "Φ(x,s) sr−1",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.09519159663865547,
        "y0": 0.6125570071258908,
        "x1": 0.9051915966386556,
        "y1": 0.6754679334916864
      },
      "text": "is strictly increasing for a.a. x ∈ Ω (i.e. (H7’) holds), then equality can occur when λ = 1 (i.e. w1 ≡ w2). If λ = 1 then for x ∈ Ω˜ (i.e. ∇w1(x) = 0) we have that Φ(x,λ|∇w1(x)|) = λr−1Φ(x,|∇w1(x)|) which rewrites as",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.09519327731092438,
        "y0": 0.6140356294536817,
        "x1": 0.41365042016806725,
        "y1": 0.6342802850356295
      },
      "text": "If we know that the function (0,∞) ∋ s  →",
      "html": null,
