      },
      "text": "is impossible to hold from the strict monotony of the function involved there. So |Ω˜| = 0 which means that ∇w1 = 0 a.e. on Ω. Therefore ∇w2 = λ∇w1 = 0 a.e. on Ω. Finally, since Ω is connected we have that w1 and w2 are diﬀerent constant functions. The theorem is now completely proved.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
